# Every endpoint, in the order a reader would try them, against the compose stack
# (docker compose up -d --build). The keys below are the demo project's, which compose.yaml seeds; they are
# public on purpose and only good on localhost.

@api = http://localhost:5180
@write = thw_demo_write_key_do_not_use_outside_localhost
@read = thr_demo_read_key_do_not_use_outside_localhost
@operator = demo-operator-token
@demo = 0199b6a0-0000-7000-8000-00000000d3e0

### Health. Ready means this collector has a catalog and can reach Kafka; ClickHouse is not part of it.
GET {{api}}/health/ready

### Send one event. 202 means it is in Kafka, not yet queryable. Replace the timestamp with a recent one:
### events older than two hours are stored as late, and older than 90 days are quarantined.
POST {{api}}/v1/events
Authorization: Bearer {{write}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messageId": "http-file-1",
  "event": "signup",
  "userId": "ada",
  "timestamp": "2026-09-23T12:00:00.000Z",
  "properties": { "plan": "pro", "source": "newsletter" }
}

### Send it again. Same messageId: acknowledged, reported as a duplicate, stored once.
POST {{api}}/v1/events
Authorization: Bearer {{write}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messageId": "http-file-1",
  "event": "signup",
  "userId": "ada",
  "timestamp": "2026-09-23T12:00:00.000Z",
  "properties": { "plan": "pro", "source": "newsletter" }
}

### A batch of up to 500. The second event has a property its schema does not declare, so it is
### quarantined; the first is accepted. The response lists every event that was not accepted, by index.
POST {{api}}/v1/events/batch
Authorization: Bearer {{write}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "events": [
    { "messageId": "http-file-2", "event": "activate", "userId": "ada", "timestamp": "2026-09-23T12:05:00.000Z" },
    { "messageId": "http-file-3", "event": "page_view", "userId": "ada", "timestamp": "2026-09-23T12:06:00.000Z", "properties": { "path": "/", "utm": "spring" } }
  ]
}

### The event types this project accepts.
GET {{api}}/v1/schemas
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}

### What is waiting in quarantine, newest first, with the reason.
GET {{api}}/v1/quarantine?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}

### Grow the page_view schema so the quarantined event would be accepted. Adding an optional property is
### allowed in place; removing one, changing a type or narrowing allowed values is refused with 409.
PUT {{api}}/v1/projects/{{demo}}/schemas/page_view/versions/1
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "properties": {
    "path": { "type": "string", "required": true },
    "referrer": { "type": "string" },
    "utm": { "type": "string" }
  }
}

### Replay it. Take the id from the quarantine list above. Lateness is judged as of when it first arrived.
POST {{api}}/v1/projects/{{demo}}/quarantine/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/replay
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}

### A funnel: users who did every step in order within the window, with the median time to each step.
POST {{api}}/v1/queries/funnel
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "steps": ["signup", "activate", "purchase"], "from": "2026-09-01", "to": "2026-09-30", "windowSeconds": 604800 }

### Retention: cohorts by the day of their first signup, and how many viewed a page each day after.
POST {{api}}/v1/queries/retention
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startEvent": "signup", "returnEvent": "page_view", "from": "2026-09-01", "to": "2026-09-30", "days": 7 }

### The same from the raw events instead of the rollup. The answer is identical; only the cost differs.
POST {{api}}/v1/queries/retention
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startEvent": "signup", "returnEvent": "page_view", "from": "2026-09-01", "to": "2026-09-30", "days": 7, "source": "events" }

### Daily counts with a property filter. Operators: eq, neq, in, gt, lt. Late events are reported apart.
POST {{api}}/v1/queries/segment
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event": "purchase", "from": "2026-09-01", "to": "2026-09-30", "filters": [{ "property": "currency", "operator": "in", "values": ["EUR", "TRY"] }] }

### Sessions per day: 30-minute inactivity gap, cut at midnight UTC.
POST {{api}}/v1/queries/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "from": "2026-09-01", "to": "2026-09-30" }

### Create a project. The keys are shown once, here, and only their hashes are stored.
POST {{api}}/v1/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "shop", "settings": { "redactProperties": ["email"], "sampleRates": { "page_view": 0.1 } } }

### Change what a project redacts and samples.
PUT {{api}}/v1/projects/{{demo}}/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "redactProperties": ["email"], "sampleRates": {} }
